      ":question/problem": "![](images/e3/e3614ea1954f36435eb1ab5f52c04d4fa3062ac337eccf76a5b47e4a03a64a1b.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i-2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=-i+j.$"
    },
