      ":question/id": "b6a55635-2f53-567e-bc46-3d92630e23fd",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-122637",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/72/721252c30370d98fe776ca00e43fef9c95a5a074140dfbdf2a00be19a66b4a1e.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is zero for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=4\\,i,\\,K(x,y)=-3\\,i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=2\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=-5\\,j.$"
