      ":question/problem": "![](images/51/51ee68a4b95a815cc9372c4d6c1b739464de223375fa301d4cf3cdb1e6e5e829.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=i+j,\\,K(x,y)=x\\,i+j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=-i+j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=-2\\,i+y\\,j.$"
